  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="about-approach-heading">
    <div class="container split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Our starting point</p><h2 id="about-approach-heading">Start with the work. Build what helps.</h2></div>
      <div class="stack"><p>A crew member needs mobile data after landing. An agent needs a clearer way to coordinate a crew change. A maritime professional needs a focused place to prepare and find useful information.</p><p>These practical needs connect the work at Amicus. The eSIM store, crew-change application and maritime resources each address a different part of life and work around shipping.</p><p>Our outlook is specialist and hands-on: understand the problem, make the next step easier, and improve the tool as the work becomes clearer.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section-soft" aria-labelledby="about-principles-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">How we approach the work</p><h2 id="about-principles-heading">Useful before complicated.</h2></div>
      <div class="grid-three">
        <article class="feature-card"><h3>Keep the maritime context.</h3><p>Port calls, international travel and crew changes have different constraints from an ordinary day at a desk. The context should shape the tool.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><h3>Make the next step clear.</h3><p>Finding a plan, opening a tool or asking a question should take a few clear steps, even from a phone during a busy journey.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><h3>Be specific about what is offered.</h3><p>Clear plan information, practical instructions and a direct conversation about requirements are more useful than broad promises.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
